From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Carlos Duran <15650777+carlos-duran@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] LAN: sessions for a local wireless game (the host's waits,
 late joiners, one session after another, a game tag, leaving)

What a frontend needs to run melonDS's LAN through a whole local wireless game, and to start, change and end
sessions while the game runs (BananaDS's in-game LAN page and its automatic mode). Every message on the wire is
melonDS's own, so a peer without this patch (desktop melonDS 1.0/1.1) plays along.

- The host waited MPRecvTimeout for a reply from every player connected to the LAN session, so a player connected
  but not in the game's DS group (its menu open, between races) stalled every MP frame (~38 fps for ~16 s). It now
  waits only for the players in its group: a player counts once it sends an auth/association request or an MP
  reply, and stops counting after 20 missed replies in a row, when its wifi powers off or when it leaves. Non-MP
  frames that arrive while it waits are requeued instead of dropped. (MyMAC: our own DS MAC, learned from our
  beacons and MP commands, so that only requests addressed to us count.)
- A player learns that another's DS wifi is on only from the Cmd_PlayerConnect sent when it turns on, so one that
  joined the session later took the host for gone at its first MP command. Whoever has its wifi on now sends its
  Cmd_PlayerConnect to each player that joins (a host to a new client, a client to the host and to another
  client's direct link).
- Accessors for the frontend: Wifi::InMPMode(), Wifi::IsPoweredOn(), LAN::GetMPActiveBitmask() and
  GetOtherPlayersBitmask().
- One session after another in the same run: EndSession clears the old session's players, connected and
  MP-active bits, miss counts and last host. The discovery socket gets SO_REUSEADDR, so discovery can run beside
  a host or restart right after a session ends.
- A game tag in the discovery beacon, its layout and size unchanged: SetDiscoveryTag() puts "BDS", a version, the
  game code, flags and a random nonce after the NUL that ends SessionName (offset 40; the visible name is cut to
  39 characters then), which melonDS without this patch never reads; ReadDiscoveryTag() reads it back.
  SetDiscoveryStatus() fills the beacon's Status (0 idle, 1 playing), which melonDS's LAN dialog already shows.
  SetHostListens(true) lets a host hear the other hosts' beacons (off by default).
- Leaving: EndSession queued an ENet disconnect for each peer and destroyed the host at once, so the others
  dropped us only when ENet timed out, seconds later. It now flushes the disconnects and services the host until
  they are acknowledged, 300 ms at most.
- "[diag]" traces of the LAN traffic, the connected bits and a per-second summary (Debug level, rate-limited).
